Frequently asked questions

Which Korean legal documents can you translate?

You can send contracts, court papers, witness statements, powers of attorney and corporate records. We translate them between English and Korean. Tell us the document type and purpose so we can match you with a legal linguist.

Can you provide a certified Korean translation for UK courts?

Yes, we can provide certified translations for use in legal proceedings. Check with your solicitor or the court about its requirements. Tell us where you will submit the document and we will advise on the format.

Do you translate documents for the Home Office?

Yes, we can translate Korean documents that you need to submit to the Home Office. These may include birth certificates, marriage certificates and police records. Check the current guidance for your application and tell us what it asks for.

How do you handle confidential legal material?

We treat your documents as confidential and limit access to the team on your project. Law firms and individuals can ask us to sign a non-disclosure agreement. Tell us about any special handling when you request a quote.

Who coordinates my legal translation project?

A dedicated project manager works with you and the translators. They answer your questions, keep the project on track and check that you have what you need. You always have a clear contact.
